}}The '''Mazarico-Narrows Bridge''' ({{Langx|bl|Ponte Mazarico-Estrechos}}), opened in 1934 and officially known as the '''First Narrows Bridge''', is a [[W:Double-deck bridge|double-decked]] [[W:Suspension bridge|suspension bridge]] that connects the [[Boroughs of Castejón|boroughs]] of [[Hisbanya]] on the west shore with [[Trinacria]] on the east shore. The term "Narrows" refers to the [[Salto Narrows]], a body of water linking [[Castejón Harbor]] (Lower Salto Bay), with the remainder of [[Salto Bay]].

The total length of the bridge including the east approach is {{convert|3,489|m|ft|0}}. The length of the suspension span is {{convert|2,020|m|ft|0}}, the main span alone is {{convert|1,280|m|ft|0}}, the tower height is {{convert|212|m|ft|0}}, and it has a ship's clearance of {{convert|68|m|ft|0}}.

The bridge has four lanes on the upper deck, with two of them being dedicated [[W:Bus lane|bus lanes]]. The lower deck has a [[W:Double-track railway|double-track rail]] line, The traffic volume on the bridge is 130,000–170,000 vehicles per day. The bridge forms part of ''Autopistas'' 1 and 17.

On 1 October 2008, the Mazarico-Narrows Bridge was designated a [[Bien de Interés Cultural|National Historic Site of Balisca]].

